  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING AMUR TIGERS VIA COMMUNITY-LED ENGAGEMENT IN NORTHEAST CHINA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO FOSTER AMUR TIGER POPULATION RECOVERY IN NORTHEAST CHINA VIA INTEGRATION OF COMMUNITY STAKEHOLDER NEEDS INTO THE CONSERVATION PROCESS. GRANTEE WILL INITIATE A THREE-YEAR PROGRAM THAT FOSTERS IMPROVED COMMUNICATION BETWEEN PARK AUTHORITIES AND LOCAL RESIDENTS BY INVITING VILLAGERS TO DIRECTLY PARTICIPATE IN TIGER CONSERVATION, AND IN RETURN THE GOVERNMENT WILL PROVIDE FUNDS AS INCENTIVES THAT WILL IMPROVE QUALITY OF LIFE IN THESE VILLAGES. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE THE FOLLOWING: (1) DEVELOP A FRAMEWORK FOR COMMUNITY-LED CONSERVATION (2) ROLL OUT THESE COMMUNITY-LED CONSERVATION TEAMS IN TWO DIFFERENT PARTS OF HUNCHUN MUNICIPAL BRANCH BUREAU AND (3) EXPAND THESE COMMUNITY-LED CONSERVATION INITIATIVES TO OTHER SUB-BUREAUS OF THE PARK.</narrative>
  </description>
